      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Absolutley. Obad's people, known as the Dragontales, thrive in the dense, untamed jungles where wild spirits are believed to guide their every move. Their culture is deeply rooted in primal connections to nature, passionate tribal rituals, and an unbending respect for the hand of fate. Unlike the Empire, whose scholars house their knowledge in rigid institutions and lofty libraries, the Dragontales gather around crackling fires, where wisdom is passed down orally, resembling tribal parables of old.\n\nInhabiting isolated communities, the Dragontales display fierce loyalty and raw emotional intensity. They value courage and physical prowess over the Empire's focus on mental prowess and strategy. Obad’s temperament is guided by passionate fervor rather than cold calculation. He leads with a compelling emotionality that stirs the hearts of his followers, resulting in uncompromising unit cohesion. Their hierarchy revolves around charismatic leaders, and the ties binding them to Obad transcend mere obligation, extending into genuine emotional allegiance.\n\nTheir spiritual beliefs differ starkly as well. Having no connection to the advanced magic of the Empire, they rely instead on spirits, deities, and omens the forests provide. Their rituals often revolve around communion with these spirits, employing",
